        "quote": "我已在CareLoop登记急诊追踪"
      }
    ],
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00081",
        "explanation": "Doctor explicitly identifies that albumin alone cannot rule out cardiac or renal risk and that missing ECG/troponin/renal results should not delay evaluation.",
        "quote": "药袋和化验单原件…由急诊医生/护士现场核对"
      }
    ],
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00058",
        "explanation": "Doctor gives practical, patient-specific instructions for safe transit—semi-sitting position, no self-exertion, no food/drink, and telling 120 the PCI/syncope history.",
        "quote": "路上让患者保持半坐位，松解领口裤带，全程不要自己用力"
      }
    ]
  },
  "dimension_ratings": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": "excellent",
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": "excellent",
    "continuity_memory_focus": "excellent",
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": "excellent",
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": "excellent"
  },
  "high_order_assessment": [
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00081",
          "explanation": "Doctor lists the specific unresolved threads that must be evaluated offline: ECG, troponin, renal function, medication reconciliation, and the unknown syncope cause. This goes beyond a simple ED referral and qualifies as bounded safe closure.",
          "quote": "把药袋+化验单交给急救员，并告诉他们阿司匹林是否已吃"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00081",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly states that the exact cause of syncope cannot be determined online and requires offline clinician evaluation, carrying forward unresolved risks.",
          "quote": "我已在CareLoop登记急诊追踪，到院后第一时间做心电图、肌钙蛋白"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO1 was triggered near the end of the encounter when the family had received the plan and the doctor needed to close the online task safely. The doctor explicitly distinguished the current handoff (going to 胸痛中心/急诊 now) from final diagnosis, listed unresolved risks (unknown syncope cause, unavailable ECG/troponin/renal results, uncertain medication regimen), specified materials to bring (records, medication packages), provided safety-net instructions, and did not close as 'problem solved' or routine follow-up. These actions are beyond the minimum handoff and receipt required by RC6/RC7 and constitute meaningful trajectory impact.",
      "ho_id": "HO1",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00081",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly corrects the family's reliance on partial albumin results by stating that missing key results should not delay urgent evaluation, and the family acknowledges by agreeing to go to 胸痛中心.",
          "quote": "药袋和手上的化验单我都塞包里带着，到急诊给医生护士看原件"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "not_completed",
      "explanation": "HO2 was partially triggered when the family hesitated about the patient refusing to go, but the doctor did not tailor the plan to that specific barrier (patient refusal) nor confirm a workable transport plan beyond generic instructions. The family merely stated they would follow the plan, which does not meet the adaptive barrier-solving criteria for completion.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "HO3 was not triggered because the doctor used workspace queries to discover hidden record context (prior acute coronary syndrome, STEMI, stent implantation, medication orders), but this discovery did not change the explanation, handoff preparation, or safety planning beyond what was already required by RC2/RC3. The family account remained vague, and the doctor did not actively integrate newly surfaced details into a revised handoff or medication reconciliation; the discovered context merely reinforced the minimum urgency duty.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00081",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly corrects the misconception that normal albumin or partial results mean the patient is safe, by directing the family to go to ED and not wait for missing results.",
          "quote": "到院后第一时间做心电图、肌钙蛋白，我这边会同步结果"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00081",
          "explanation": "Family acknowledges the corrected plan by confirming they will go to 胸痛中心 with records and will not self-administer uncertain medications.",
          "quote": "药没我没敢乱给，硝酸甘油我分不清是哪一个"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO4 was triggered when the family expressed the misconception that the albumin result looked normal and the patient's recovery meant it was safe. The doctor actively corrected this by explaining that albumin alone cannot establish safety and that missing ECG/troponin/renal results should not delay urgent evaluation. The family acknowledged the correction by agreeing to go to 胸痛中心 with the records and explicitly stating they would not self-medicate. This active correction changed the family's behavior and is beyond the minimum warning required by RC3/RC5.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    }
  ],
